window.LOT_NEW={"id": "l20261117", "label": "Lot du 17 novembre 2026", "accounts": [{"id": "cade", "handle": "@cade.plum", "caption": "The work nobody posts happens in the quiet hours. The cold track under a streetlight, the last pull up when your grip is almost gone, the late night at the desk long after everyone has gone to bed. None of it looks impressive in the moment, and almost none of it gets filmed. That is exactly why it matters. It is the part that belongs to you, with no audience and no applause, just a promise you keep when it would be easier to skip. Over weeks it turns into a version of you that feels steady and earned. You do not have to prove anything to anyone. You only have to show up again tomorrow and do the same unglamorous things again.\n\n#discipline #grind #motivation #selfimprovement #focus", "video": "l20261117-cade-web.mp4", "poster": "l20261117-cade-poster.jpg", "slides": []}, {"id": "lena", "handle": "@lena.fit2", "caption": "Skipped Monday's workout? The week is not ruined. This is the moment where many of us decide the whole plan has failed, when really it is just one missed session in a long stretch of good intentions. Go on Wednesday instead. Pack your bag the night before, put the headphones in, and pick the machines you actually enjoy. Keep it gentle if you need to, because twenty easy minutes still count more than a perfect session that never happens. Pick up where you left off, not where you think you should be by now. Showing up late is still showing up, and the habit is still yours. Be kind to yourself and let tomorrow feel a little lighter than today did.\n\n#gymgirl #fitnessjourney #consistency #gymmotivation #selfcare", "slides": ["l20261117-lena-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-lena-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-lena-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-lena-slide-04.jpg", "l20261117-lena-slide-05.jpg"]}, {"id": "cyra", "handle": "@cyra.volt4", "caption": "Sunday evening without the dread is possible, and it usually comes from a few small things done on purpose. Put fresh sheets on the bed so the night feels like a gift. Take a walk before dark and let the light settle your thoughts. Pack tomorrow's bag and set your shoes next to it so the morning has fewer decisions waiting. Light a candle, open a book and let the evening slow down on its own. None of this needs to be perfect or beautiful for anyone else. It only needs to make Monday feel lighter when it arrives. And if the week still starts loudly, that is fine too. Monday can wait until Monday.\n\n#sundayreset #slowliving #selfcare #cozyhome #weeklyreset", "slides": ["l20261117-cyra-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-cyra-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-cyra-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-cyra-slide-04.jpg", "l20261117-cyra-slide-05.jpg"]}, {"id": "restart", "handle": "@user7658638327909", "caption": "You missed October 1st. That is fine. Your winter arc can start today, and it does not need a big announcement or a perfect plan. It needs a few rules you will actually follow. Train four days a week and stop negotiating with yourself about it. Walk every day, even when it is cold and grey outside. Keep your phone out of the bedroom so the night belongs to sleep. Be in bed before midnight, because recovery is where the progress happens. And do not announce any of it. Just start quietly, show up on the boring days, and let the weeks pile up behind you. Late is still earlier than never, and there are still plenty of days left this year. Save this for the day you need the reminder.\n\n#winterarc #discipline #gymmotivation #lockin #consistency", "slides": ["l20261117-restart-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-restart-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-restart-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-restart-slide-04.jpg", "l20261117-restart-slide-05.jpg", "l20261117-restart-slide-06.jpg"]}, {"id": "royal", "handle": "@royal.discipline7", "caption": "What I keep on my desk now is much smaller than it used to be. One notebook. One pen that works. A lamp instead of a screen, so the room stays calm after dark. Water within reach so I do not have to leave the page. The phone sits face down across the room, far enough that picking it up takes a real decision. None of this is about looking organised for anyone else. It is about removing the small interruptions that quietly eat an evening, so that the thinking and the writing can actually happen. Less on the desk, more on the page. Try clearing yours tonight and see how much easier it feels to begin.\n\n#deskroutine #focus #journaling #darkacademia #minimalism", "slides": ["l20261117-royal-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-royal-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-royal-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-royal-slide-04.jpg", "l20261117-royal-slide-05.jpg", "l20261117-royal-slide-06.jpg", "l20261117-royal-slide-07.jpg"]}, {"id": "consistent", "handle": "@consistent.lifest", "caption": "Wednesday, and nothing went to plan? The week is not over. Work ran late, the schedule slipped and the workout you planned did not happen. That is normal, and it says nothing about your discipline. Train for twenty minutes today, even if it is a shorter version of the usual session. Make one real dinner and sit down to eat it like a person with a plan. Then go to bed at a reasonable time and let tomorrow start fresh. Consistency is not a perfect streak, it is the habit of coming back without drama. Three good days still make a good week, and you still have more than enough time left to get there.\n\n#consistency #healthyhabits #fitness #weeklyroutine #selfcare", "slides": ["l20261117-consistent-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-consistent-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-consistent-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-consistent-slide-04.jpg", "l20261117-consistent-slide-05.jpg"]}, {"id": "undeniable", "handle": "@undeniable.lifest", "caption": "Sunday, 4 PM. You can spend it watching someone else's weekend through a screen, or you can have your own. It feels like rest to scroll, but most of the time it leaves you a little emptier and a little more tired than before. The other option takes more effort at the start and gives far more back, a table full of friends, a walk with no destination, a sunset on the sand with a ball in the air. Same Sunday, different Monday. You do not have to quit your phone forever. Just choose now and then the version of the day you will actually remember, and notice how different the evening feels when it was lived instead of watched.\n\n#sunday #intentionalliving #weekend #lifestyle #habits", "slides": ["l20261117-undeniable-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-undeniable-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-undeniable-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-undeniable-slide-04.jpg"]}, {"id": "track", "handle": "@track.discipline", "caption": "Three things I did this week instead of scrolling. A Tuesday run before work, with the sun low and the path almost empty. A real dinner on Thursday, with the table set and nobody checking a phone. A book in the sun on Saturday, long enough to forget what time it was. None of these were productive in the usual sense, and none of them would have gone viral. They were just good, and they filled the week with something worth remembering. Look back at your own week and ask what made it feel good, then make a little more room for that next time. A full life is made of small, simple moments that you actually show up for, one ordinary day after another.\n\n#slowliving #weeklyreset #habits #intentionalliving #selfimprovement", "slides": ["l20261117-track-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-track-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-track-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-track-slide-04.jpg"]}, {"id": "daily", "handle": "@daily.discipline951", "caption": "The first ten minutes after you wake up quietly set the tone for the whole day. Open the curtains before you open your phone and let the light in. Drink a full glass of water before anything else. Make the bed, and badly is absolutely fine, because the point is the small signal that your day has started on purpose. Then make the coffee and take your time with it. None of this is complicated and none of it takes more than a few minutes, but it moves your morning from reacting to choosing. When the first ten minutes belong to you, the rest of the day tends to follow along more calmly. Try it tomorrow and notice the difference.\n\n#morningroutine #dailyhabits #slowliving #selfcare #routine", "slides": ["l20261117-daily-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-daily-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-daily-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-daily-slide-04.jpg", "l20261117-daily-slide-05.jpg"]}, {"id": "good", "handle": "@good.motivation14", "caption": "I'll start on Monday. It's Thursday. What's wrong with tonight? That little exchange says more about habits than any big plan ever could. We love the idea of a fresh start, a clean week and a perfect first day, so we keep pushing the beginning further away. Meanwhile the evening is right here and it is perfectly good enough. A short walk after dinner counts. A glass of water counts. Ten quiet minutes tidying your space counts. Starting small is still starting, and it has one big advantage over waiting for Monday, which is that it actually happens. Take the first small step tonight and let Monday find you already on your way.\n\n#habits #motivation #smallsteps #selfimprovement #mindset", "slides": ["l20261117-good-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-good-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-good-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-good-slide-04.jpg"]}, {"id": "self", "handle": "@self.discipline84", "caption": "Tuesday, 6:14 PM. You said you would train. The couch is right there, and so are your shoes. This is the exact moment most plans quietly fall apart, not in the gym but in the hallway between a good intention and the first step. You do not need motivation for this part. You only need a deal small enough to say yes to. Ten minutes. That is all you owe yourself right now. Most of the time the hard part is the door, and once you are outside the rest takes care of itself. Tuesday, 6:31 PM. You went. Nobody saw it, nobody clapped, and it still counts. That is how a habit gets built, one ordinary evening at a time.\n\n#discipline #selfimprovement #habits #motivation #mindset", "slides": ["l20261117-self-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-self-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-self-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-self-slide-04.jpg", "l20261117-self-slide-05.jpg"]}, {"id": "club", "handle": "@clubclff8lx", "caption": "Nobody is going to do it for you. Not your friends, not your plans, and definitely not tomorrow. People love to wait for the right moment, the right mood or the right group to start with them, but the work has always been yours alone. Nobody can do the reps in your place, nobody can eat well on your behalf, and nobody can wake up for you when the alarm goes off. That sounds harsh, but it is also the best news you will hear today, because it means the result is entirely in your hands as well. The work is yours. So is the result. Start with whatever is closest to you and do it today, without waiting for anyone to join you.\n\n#discipline #mindset #gym #selfdiscipline #focus", "slides": ["l20261117-club-slide-01.jpg", "l20261117-club-slide-02.jpg", "l20261117-club-slide-03.jpg", "l20261117-club-slide-04.jpg"]}, {"id": "energized", "handle": "@energized.discipl", "caption": "You don't need to feel like it. You need to lace your shoes and open the door. Most days the feeling shows up about ten minutes after you start, never before, which is why waiting for it keeps so many people stuck at home. Motivation is a result, not a requirement. So when your legs feel heavy and the sky looks grey, keep the plan small and simple. One easy run, one steady pace, one foot in front of the other until the day starts to feel lighter. Nobody has to watch and nobody has to know. Just move, and let the energy follow you instead of waiting for it to arrive first. Tired is a feeling. Going anyway is a decision.\n\n#running #runmotivation #discipline #mindset #justgo", "video": "l20261117-energized-web.mp4", "poster": "l20261117-energized-poster.jpg", "slides": []}]};